Z||000000||Alex2004||05-09-2001||10:17 PM||||Is the ajar light in the front compartment supposed to come on whenever the decklid is open? or when parking/headlights are on w/ it open?  I wondered b4 why it never came on w/ the deck open with no lights on, and then once i noticed when i opened it w/ parking lights on, it was on, and it went off when i turned it off... Is it supposed to work like this?  I know trunk light doesn't.  Let me know<P>Thanks..<BR>Alex...||||reg||1
Z||000001||jaguiler||05-09-2001||10:20 PM||||you might want to chk the wiring harness from the firewall that attaches to the decklid.  these wires often melt.  I just repaired mine....<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||05-09-2001||10:40 PM||||It is supposed to work just as you described - only when the parking lights are on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||05-10-2001||06:53 AM||||Yes, the accessory light in the front compartment comes on any time that the front  'hood' is open, AND the parking lights are on.<P>Both conditions must be met for the light to be on - just one or the other won't do it. <P>That's the way it properly works from the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||05-10-2001||07:27 AM||||If you are asking about the door ajar light on the dash, my 87 has a switch that turns the door ajar light on when the hood is open.  To keep costs down on the 88, Pontiac removed the hood switch.<P>I'm not sure about other years.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT GT 87||05-10-2001||08:23 PM||||The light you describe is for you to look for things when it is dark...........  Thus it only is on when the head lites or parking lites are on .. The door ajar is on the dashboard .......... Steve||||reg||1
